'''Canara HSBC Life Insurance''' is an Indian [[life insurance]] company, headquartered in Gurugram.<ref>{{cite news |title=Canara Bank, life insurance arm launch 'Webassurance' |url=https://www.businesstoday.in/sectors/banks/canara-bank-canara-hsbc-oriental-bank-of-commerce-life-insurance-canara-hsbc-obc-life-r-a-sankara-narayanan/story/341062.html |publisher=[[Business Today (India)|Business Today]] |date=27 April 2019}}</ref> Established in 2008, Canara HSBC Life Insurance <ref name=ms>{{Cite web |date=16 June 2022 |first=Mayur |last=Shetty |title=Canara HSBC Life rebrands due to PNB exit|url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/canara-hsbc-life-rebrands-due-to-pnb-exit/articleshow/92239213.cms |access-date=2022-06-17 |website=The Times of India |language=en}}</ref> was a [[joint venture]] between [[Canara Bank]] (36.5%), [[HSBC Insurance (Asia Pacific)|HSBC Insurance (Asia Pacific) Holdings Limited]] (26%) and [[Punjab National Bank]] (23%). On 15 June 2022, the company renamed itself as Canara HSBC Life Insurance after the exit of its third partner, Punjab National Bank.<ref name=ms/><ref name="livemint.com">{{Cite web |date=2022-06-15 |title=Canara HSBC OBC Life Insurance rebranded as Canara HSBC Life Insurance |url=https://www.livemint.com/companies/news/canara-hsbc-obc-life-insurance-rebranded-as-canara-hsbc-life-insurance-11655294928414.html |access-date=2022-06-17 |website=mint |language=en}}</ref>

The company provides life, health, online term plans, credit life and employee benefit segments.<ref>{{cite news |title=Bank Merger: 6 things OBC, UBI customers should know about debit cards, cheque books to passbooks post merger with PNB |url=https://www.zeebiz.com/personal-finance/news-bank-merger-6-things-obc-ubi-customers-should-know-about-debit-cards-cheque-books-to-passbooks-post-merger-with-pnb-123963 |publisher=[[zeebiz.com]]|date=13 April 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Amalgamation of Oriental Bank of Commerce and United Bank of India into Punjab National Bank|url=https://www.pnbindia.in/downloadprocess.aspx?fid=Zu0vAs1Rv/cicTxP88flVQ== |website=Punjab National Bank}}</ref>

== History and overview  ==
The company was established in 2008. In February 2014, Canara HSBC Life Insurance <ref name="livemint.com"/> introduced the concept of online revival of the policy, enabling customers to reinstate a lapsed policy and allowing them to pay their [[Premium financing|premium]] online.<ref>{{cite news |title=HSBC Oriental Bank of Commerce Life Insurance Company launches online revival of policies |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/wealth/personal-finance-news/hsbc-oriental-bank-of-commerce-life-insurance-company-launches-online-revival-of-policies/articleshow/30991463.cms?from=mdrhttps://economictimes.indiatimes.com/wealth/personal-finance-news/hsbc-oriental-bank-of-commerce-life-insurance-company-launches-online-revival-of-policies/articleshow/30991463.cms?from=mdr |publisher=[[The Economic Times]] |date=25 February 2014}}</ref>

It partnered with 3 rural regional banks, Pragathi Gramin Bank in [[Karnataka]] and Shreyas Gramin Bank in [[Uttar Pradesh]] in 2009 and [[South Malabar Gramin Bank]] in 2010.<ref>{{cite web|title=Introduction|url=https://www.https://www.canarahsbclife.com/lifeinsurance/portal/canh/home/about-us/why-choose-us.com/lifeinsurance/portal/canh/home/about-us/why-choose-us|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130819141428/http://https/|archive-date=2013-08-19|access-date=2020-07-12|website=Canarahsbclife.com}}</ref> The company partnered with [[Dhanlaxmi Bank]] in June 2017.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Kumar |first1=Krishna |title=Canara HSBC Oriental Bank of Commerce Life Insurance ties up with Dhanlaxmi Bank |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/industry/banking/finance/banking/canara-hsbc-oriental-bank-of-commerce-life-insurance-ties-up-with-dhanlaxmi-bank/articleshow/59473611.cms |publisher=[[The Economic Times]] |date=6 June 2017}}</ref> It also tied up with Can Fin Homes and<ref>{{cite news |title=Canara HSBC OBC Life Insurance partners Can Fin Homes to sell policies |url=https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/business/canara-hsbc-obc-life-insurance-partners-can-fin-homes-to-sell-policies-2523861.html |publisher=[[Moneycontrol.com]]|date=8 March 2018}}</ref> IndianMoneyInsurance.com.<ref>{{cite news |title=Canara HSBC OBC Life Insurance partners with IndianMoneyInsurance.com to sell policies |url=https://www.freepressjournal.in/insurance/insurance-top-news/canara-hsbc-obc-life-insurance-partners-with-indianmoneyinsurancecom-to-sell-policies |publisher=[[The Free Press Journal]] |date=17 October 2019}}</ref> In April 2020, [[Oriental Bank of Commerce]] merged with Punjab National Bank.<ref>{{Cite web|date=30 August 2019|title=Bank Merger News: Government unveils mega bank mergers to revive growth from 5-year low|url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/government-unveils-mega-bank-mergers-to-revive-growth-from-5-year-low/articleshow/70911359.cms|access-date=2021-10-08|website=The Times of India|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|author=Staff Writer|date=2019-08-30|title=10 public sector banks to be merged into four|url=https://www.livemint.com/news/india/pnb-obc-and-united-bank-to-be-merged-nirmala-sitharaman-1567158678718.html|access-date=2021-10-08|website=mint|language=en}}</ref> On 15 June 2022, the company rebranded as Canara HSBC Life Insurance.<ref name="freepressjournal.in">{{Cite web |title=Canara HSBC OBC Life Insurance renews commitment to its customers with Canara HSBC Life Insurance rebranding |url=https://www.freepressjournal.in/business/canara-hsbc-life-insurance-rebrands-itself |access-date=2022-06-17 |website=Free Press Journal |language=en}}</ref>

